<point name="coop_spawnpoint" color="0 1 0" box="-18 -18 -24 18 18 48">
Potential spawning position for COOP

Target with 'coop_spawnpoint_trigger' or tick the box 'startactive' to activate the spawn. Always pick a team (allies or axis).

"targetname" if targeted by 'coop_spawnpoint_trigger'
"angle" facing direction
<flag key="StartActive" name="StartActive" bit="0"/>
<flag key="Allied" name="Allied" bit="1"/>
<flag key="Axis" name="Axis" bit="2"/>
</point>

<point name="coop_spawnpoint_trigger" color="0 1 0" box="-16 -16 -16 16 16 16">
Captureable flag. Target it to 'coop_spawnpoint' and 'target_location'.

"target" target it to 'coop_spawnpoint' (and 'target_location')
"model" add model ( models/multiplayer/flagpole/flagpole_reinforce.md3 )
"angle" facing direction

It is possible to give each flag an individual name that is printed if you capture the flag

Naming your flag is handy and simple: use 'target_location'
</point>

<point name="target_location" color="0 0.5 0" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
Names an area. In SP the closest one in sight (else closest by distance) is used for
kill/location messages; in COOP it can be linked to a coop_spawnpoint_trigger to name a flag.

"message"    name of the location
"count"      colour 0-7 (0:white 1:red 2:green 3:yellow 4:blue 5:cyan 6:magenta 7:white)
"targetname" set so a coop_spawnpoint_trigger can display this name on capture
</point>

<group name="func_train" color="0 .5 .8">
A train is a mover that moves between path_corner target points.
Trains MUST HAVE AN ORIGIN BRUSH.
The train spawns at the first target it is pointing at.
"model2"	.md3 model to also draw
"speed"		default 100
"dmg"		default 2
"noise"		looping sound to play when the train is in motion
"target"	next path corner
"color"		constantLight color
"light"		constantLight radius
<flag key="START_ON" name="START_ON" bit="0"/>
<flag key="TOGGLE" name="TOGGLE" bit="1"/>
<flag key="BLOCK_STOPS" name="BLOCK_STOPS" bit="2"/>
</group>

<group name="func_secret" color="0 .5 .8">
A one-shot sliding door: on trigger it slides aside (opposite its angle) and stays open.
REVERSE		slide toward the angle instead of away from it
CRUSHER		does not back off when blocked
TOUCH		spawn a touch field so the player opens it by walking into it

"key"		-1 for locked, key number for which key opens, 0 for open (default '0' unless door is targeted)
"model2"	.md3 model to also draw
"angle"		determines the opening direction
"targetname" if set, no touch field is spawned; a remote button or trigger activates it
"speed"		movement speed (100 default)
"wait"		wait before returning (2 default, -1 = never return)
"lip"		lip remaining at end of move (8 default)
"dmg"		damage to inflict when blocked (2 default)
"color"		constantLight color
"light"		constantLight radius
"health"	if set, the door must be shot open
<flag key="REVERSE" name="REVERSE" bit="0"/>
<flag key="CRUSHER" name="CRUSHER" bit="2"/>
<flag key="TOUCH" name="TOUCH" bit="3"/>
</group>

<group name="func_tramcar" color="0 .5 .8">
A tramcar is a damageable mover that runs between path_corner points.
health value of 999 designates a piece as non-damageable.
The LEADER of a tramcar group MUST have the LEADER flag set. When the Leader's health
hits zero it unlinks and the team becomes visible.
All tramcar parts MUST HAVE AN ORIGIN BRUSH. The tramcar spawns at the first target it points at.
Place it in its END position when compiling, then start it by targeting the desired path_corner.
"model2"	.md3 model to also draw
"speed"		default 100
"dmg"		default 2
"noise"		looping sound to play when in motion
"target"	next path corner
"color"		constantLight color
"light"		constantLight radius
"type"		debris type when destroyed ("glass", "wood", "metal", "gibs") default "wood"
"mass"		debris amount, default 75 (one large chunk per 100 mass up to 8, one small per 25 up to 16)
<flag key="START_ON" name="START_ON" bit="0"/>
<flag key="TOGGLE" name="TOGGLE" bit="1"/>
<flag key="LEADER" name="LEADER" bit="3"/>
</group>

<group name="func_train_particles" color="0.3 0.1 0.8">
Brush that emits a particle stream while enabled. Target an info_notnull for direction.
"health"	particle count, default 16
<flag key="START_ON" name="START_ON" bit="0"/>
<flag key="TOGGLE" name="TOGGLE" bit="1"/>
</group>

<point name="func_bats" color="0.3 0.1 0.8" box="-32 -32 -32 32 32 32">
Spawns a flock of bats/spirits that fly a waypoint path.
"count"		number of bats (default 10)
"radius"	maximum distance from the entity centre to place each bat (default 32)
"speed"		travel speed to the next waypoint (default 300)
"wait"		(end-map) seconds between spawning
"target"	(end-map) distance-check entity; spawning enables when the player is more than "radius" from it
"delay"		(end-map) seconds after the player steps outside before spirits spawn
<flag key="START_ON" name="START_ON" bit="0"/>
<flag key="TOGGLE" name="TOGGLE" bit="1"/>
<flag key="END_OUTER" name="END_OUTER" bit="2"/>
</point>

<group name="props_flippy_table" color=".8 .6 .2">
A table that flips over when triggered. Needs a LEADER part and an origin brush.
Place the origin brush so the leader and slave flip over correctly.
X_AXIS / Y_AXIS - axis to flip around
<flag key="X_AXIS" name="X_AXIS" bit="2"/>
<flag key="Y_AXIS" name="Y_AXIS" bit="3"/>
<flag key="LEADER" name="LEADER" bit="4"/>
</group>

<group name="truck_cam" color=".7 .3 .1">
Camera mover that rides a path_corner track (used with the truck cinematic).
"target"	first path corner
"count2"	on a path_corner, controls playback of gear-change sounds
<flag key="START_ON" name="START_ON" bit="0"/>
<flag key="TOGGLE" name="TOGGLE" bit="1"/>
</group>

<point name="misc_landmine" color="1 0 0" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
A pre-armed landmine, independent of the engineer class and the landmine weapon/ammo.
On spawn it drops to the floor beneath it and detonates when a hostile AI walks into its trigger radius.
INVISIBLE		no marker flag, and the mine can't be seen at all
START_OFF		spawns inert; a targeting entity (func_invisible_user, trigger_*, ...) must arm it
TRIGGER_PLAYERS	also detonates on players (default: hostile AI only)
TOUCH_EXPLO		blow the instant something steps on it (default: blow when it steps back off)
"wait"		seconds before the mine re-arms itself after going off (default 0 = never re-arms)
"dmg"		splash damage override (default: standard landmine damage)
"radius"	splash radius override (default 200)
"targetname" so a func_invisible_user / trigger can (re)arm it
Minefield for sale: give every misc_landmine the same "targetname", point a func_invisible_user
(with "price", no "delay", no STARTOFF/FREE_AFTER_USE) at that targetname, and set START_OFF +
"wait" 0 on the mines. The first purchase arms the field; every later purchase re-arms just the
mines that have blown.
<flag key="INVISIBLE" name="INVISIBLE" bit="0"/>
<flag key="START_OFF" name="START_OFF" bit="1"/>
<flag key="TRIGGER_PLAYERS" name="TRIGGER_PLAYERS" bit="2"/>
<flag key="TOUCH_EXPLO" name="TOUCH_EXPLO" bit="3"/>
</point>

<point name="misc_tagemitter" color=".4 .9 .7" box="-16 -16 -16 16 16 16">
Attaches a tag/effect emitter to a script_mover.
Must target the script_mover it attaches to. 'use' toggles it on/off. An AIScript "alertentity" call kills it.
</point>

<point name="plane_waypoint" color=".5 .3 0" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
Waypoint for props_me109 aircraft paths. Fires its target when reached.
"count"	number of AIScript "alertentity" calls needed before the aircraft branches tracks
"track"	name of the track to branch to (several tracks may share a name; one is picked at random, max 8 per branch)
<flag key="SCRIPTS" name="SCRIPTS" bit="0"/>
<flag key="DIE" name="DIE" bit="1"/>
<flag key="EXPLODE" name="EXPLODE" bit="2"/>
<flag key="LAPS" name="LAPS" bit="3"/>
<flag key="ATTACK" name="ATTACK" bit="4"/>
</point>

<point name="props_me109" color=".7 .3 .1" box="-128 -128 0 128 128 64">
Scripted Me-109 aircraft that flies plane_waypoint paths.
"health"	default 1000
<flag key="START_ON" name="START_ON" bit="0"/>
<flag key="TOGGLE" name="TOGGLE" bit="1"/>
<flag key="SPINNINGPROP" name="SPINNINGPROP" bit="2"/>
<flag key="FIXED_DIE" name="FIXED_DIE" bit="3"/>
</point>

<point name="test_gas" color="0 0.5 0" box="-4 -4 -4 4 4 4">
Development/test entity that emits a gas cloud. Not for shipping maps.
</point>

<point name="target_position" color="0 0.5 0" box="-4 -4 -4 4 4 4">
Positional target, identical to info_notnull / misc_teleporter_dest.
Point teleporters, jumppads and cameras at one of these.
</point>

</classes>
